name 'designing-reliable-apps-preassessment-q11_2025'

question 'An app\'s event-ticket-availability feature fails because an external API goes down. Which design choice best maintains user trust?'

wrong 'Display the raw JavaScript error from the console so technically-minded users can diagnose the problem themselves'
wrong 'Silently hide the feature with no explanation and wait for the API to come back online'
wrong 'Automatically reload the entire page on a loop every few seconds until the API starts responding again'
right 'Show a clear, friendly message explaining what went wrong and offer the user a helpful next step, like a retry button'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 7
MARKDOWN
